<title>UK: European cotton market quietens.</title>
<headline>European cotton market quietens.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL, ENGLAND 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quieter trading conditions have prevailed on several of the European raw cotton markets in Western Europe, traders said.</p>
<p>Slow mill demand was attributable to a number of factors including firm New York futures, a firm dollar and less promising economic prospects in some European countries, they said.</p>
<p>However, spinning activity in most countries was generally well maintained. A few spinners in certain markets such as Portugal have begun looking closely at their prospective requirements for the second half of the year.</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
